Cancelling them will only stop the spellcasting, and it is easier said
than done. A wand of cancellation counts as a rather low attack level,
so an arch-lich's monster-magic-resistance will likely render it
ineffective. Frankly, it's way better to kill liches.

> An unrelated question (but one which interests me in my current
> game): if you cancel an Archlich, can it still teleport to the
> up stairs? =A0What about its other powers? =A0And do they (or anyone
> else) resist cancellation?

All it stops is spellcasting, including monster summoning. It will
still teleport, steal the amulet, cover you with frost etc.

